# Blender/rig source material — huge (.blend + backup .glb). The RUNTIME models
# live in public/; these sources stay local (back them up separately).
rig-src/
*-bones.txt
*.blend
*.blend[0-9]*

# The full source model. 155 MB, and NOTHING uses it: it is not in public/, no
# module imports it, the runtime never fetches it, and the README calls it a
# reference. It was tracked through LFS anyway, so every Vercel build pulled
# those 155 MB before compiling -- 77% of a 201 MB per-build LFS bill against a
# 1 GB/month free quota, which is five builds a month before deploys start
# failing at checkout with "over its data quota". Keep it locally and back it up
# outside the repo.
cuerpo_completo.glb

# Local Claude Code tooling / preview config
.claude/
